a</article-title><source>Toxicon</source><year>2001</year><volume>39</volume><fpage>97</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10936626</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-md-06-00456"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lawrence</surname><given-names>DN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ciguatera fish poisoning in Miami</article-title><source>J Am Med Assoc</source><year>1980</year><volume>244</volume><fpage>254</fpage><lpage>258</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b10-md-06-00456"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McKee</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physician diagnosis and reporting of ciguatera fish poisoning in an endemic area</article-title><source>Harmful Algal Blooms</source><year>2001</year><fpage>451</fpage><lpage>453</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b11-md-06-00456"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Begier</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Outbreak bias in illness reporting and case confirmation in ciguatera fish poisoning Surveillance in South Florida</article-title><source>Pub Health Rep</source><year>2006</year><volume>121</volume><fpage>658</fpage><lpage>665</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17278400</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-md-06-00456"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nicholson</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ciguatoxins: cyclic polyether modulators of voltage-gated ion channel function</article-title><source>Mar Drugs</source><year>2006</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>88</fpage><lpage>118</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b13-md-06-00456"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group p